Reinstalling a layer now creates the registry records its settings interface has gained since the site was set up. Each layer's `post_install` registers its own interface — `IIdentitySettings`, `IProfileSettings`, `IServerSettings` — under the package prefix, so a field added after a site was installed gets its record, with the schema default, and existing values are kept.

Without it a site installed before a field existed answered `KeyError` from every control panel that reads the interface, which is a 500 on `@controlpanels/identity-providers` rather than a missing checkbox. The package is unreleased and ships no upgrade steps by design, so reapplying the profile is the whole repair path and it has to actually repair something.

Provider records get the same treatment from the other end: they are now registered against `IProviderRecords`, an interface stating the five fields every provider has whatever its driver. A profile can therefore declare a provider with one `<records interface=... prefix=... />` node instead of restating a field type per record. The driver's own configuration records stay outside any interface and keep carrying their types, because which of them exist is decided by the driver at runtime and no fixed schema can describe that. @ericof
